<title>USA: Exxon says has 50 pct of Azeri oil block.</title>
<headline>Exxon says has 50 pct of Azeri oil block.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Exxon Corp said Friday it has a 50 percent  share and would operate the Nakhchivan block in Azerbaijan's sector  of the Caspian Sea, following the signing of a deal in Washington,  where Azeri president Heydar Aliev is on a state visit.</p>
<p>The block is located about 60 miles (100 km) south of Baku and 30  miles south of the existing Bulla-Deniz gas condensate field, which  had original proven reserves of about three trillion cubic feet, Exxon  said in a statement.</p>
</text>
